// GENERATED by scripts/build-sky.ts — do not edit by hand; run `npm run precompute`.
//
// The sky over eclipse day: 285 stars of magnitude 3.5 or brighter, precessed from
// their J2000 catalogue positions, plus the 5 naked-eye planets at 2026-08-12T17:45:00.000Z.
// Coordinates are of-date equatorial (RA in hours, Dec in degrees); skyObjects.ts rotates them into an
// observer's horizon frame.
//
// Deliberately anonymous: the renderer identifies nothing (it draws dots from magnitude and position),
// so names — and even the star/planet distinction — would be dead weight in the bundle. The names live
// in the SOURCE catalogue (starCatalog.ts, dev-only); tests that need to know which row is which match
// rows back to it by coordinates, and identify planets by their ephemeris positions (or, coarsely, by
// magnitude: the faintest planet here is 1.29, and only Venus passes -4).
//
// PLANET_INDEX is the one deliberate exception: the sky-view planet LABELS need to know which anonymous
// rows are which planet, and five indices are the cheapest identity that can carry that (~60 bytes,
// against the ~2 KB of names this file used to ship). Everything else stays anonymous.

